MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Chicago's Greatest Hits fits my interest in familiar classic-rock songs, reflected in my choices of The Cars and Now Classic Rock Hits.",
    "The Four Tops collection connects with my interest in older pop and AM Gold, while A Charlie Brown Christmas feels like a gentle holiday follow-up to A Very Special Christmas."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Titles such as Ultimate Collection and The Very Best Of do not tell me whose music I would hear; liking compilations does not mean I want an unfamiliar collection.",
    "Toots & The Maytals does not match the classic-rock and older-pop songs I want today. Love Somebody and Bc - White Christmas leave me too uncertain about the actual release to choose them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repeated interest in greatest-hits albums seems to have been taken as interest in almost any best-of collection, regardless of the performer.",
    "My recent Christmas selection seems to have counted as enough reason for another holiday release, even when I cannot identify whose music it contains."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Recognizing the performer and having a sense of the songs matters more to me than the collection label alone.",
    "My older-pop and classic-rock choices provide a more specific guide to what I want than simply choosing compilations; holiday music is an additional current interest."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in familiar hits and holiday listening, but leaned too heavily on compilation titles without establishing whether I would recognize and want the music."
}
